# vulnerable transitive dependencies in tar and brace-expansion.
# We do not extract untrusted archives or handle multipart uploads, so the
# vulnerable tar/brace-expansion code paths are not exercised by this service.
CVE-2026-13149 exp:2026-10-31
CVE-2026-59873 exp:2026-10-31
CVE-2026-59874 exp:2026-10-31

# vulnerable fast-uri transitive dependency mismatch with Node URL parsing.
# We do not generate arbitrary URIs from untrusted input in this service, so this
# does not create a reachable exploit path.
CVE-2026-16221 exp:2026-10-31

# vulnerable brace-expansion bundled in npm internals. The service does not call
# the affected glob expansion code at runtime, and this path is outside the app's
# dependency tree.
CVE-2026-14257 exp:2026-10-31

# vulnerability in find-my-way bundled via Fastify. This service listens on plain
# HTTP/1.1 only; it does not enable `http2: true`, so the HTTP/2 DoS code path is
# not active.
CVE-2026-47219 exp:2026-10-31

# vulnerability in fastify/static, which is in this case a dependency of
# the swagger-ui. That's only exposed internally, so we don't have to worry
# much about that.
CVE-2026-15074 exp:2026-10-31

# vulnerability in ip-address. It's in the base node image, but we're not using it.
CVE-2026-69192 exp:2026-10-31

# vulnerability in brace-expansion, in the npm internals
CVE-2026-69152 exp:2026-10-31

# vulnerability in tar, bundled inside npm itself (not our own dependency tree).
# We do not extract untrusted archives at runtime; the service only runs
# `node dist/server.js` and does not accept archive upload processing.
# Re-check when npm ships a release with tar >= 7.5.21.
CVE-2026-73566 exp:2026-10-31

# vulnerabilities in libcrypto and libssl affecting QUIC servers, which we are not using
CVE-2026-14456 exp:2026-10-31
